::: {.doc-subject}

Specify that a style value should be fetched from a column in the data.
:::

::: {.doc-usage-source}
Usage

[Source](https://github.com/posit-dev/great-tables/blob/main/great_tables/_styles.py#L21-L78){target="_blank" rel="noopener"}
:::

::: {.doc-signature .doc-Kind.CLASS}
```python
from_column(column, na_value=None, fn=None)
```
:::

## Parameters {.doc-parameters}

::: {.doc-definition-items}
<code>[column]{.doc-parameter-name}[:]{.doc-parameter-annotation-sep} [str]{.doc-parameter-annotation}</code>

:   A column name in the data containing the styling information.

<code>[na_value]{.doc-parameter-name}[:]{.doc-parameter-annotation-sep} [Any | None]{.doc-parameter-annotation} [=]{.doc-parameter-default-sep .op} [None]{.doc-parameter-default}</code>

:   A single value to replace any NA values in the column (currently not supported).

<code>[fn]{.doc-parameter-name}[:]{.doc-parameter-annotation-sep} [Callable[[Any], Any] | None]{.doc-parameter-annotation} [=]{.doc-parameter-default-sep .op} [None]{.doc-parameter-default}</code>

:   A callable applied to transform each value extracted from `column=`.
:::

## Examples {.doc-examples}

This example demonstrates styling the `"x"` column.

Style the text color using the `"color"` column:

::: {#9c4bd965 .cell execution_count=1}
``` {.python .cell-code}
import pandas as pd
import polars as pl
from great_tables import GT, from_column, loc, style, px

df = pd.DataFrame({"x": [15, 20], "color": ["red", "blue"]})

(GT(df).tab_style(style=style.text(color=from_column("color")), locations=loc.body(columns=["x"])))
```

